#====================================================================
# Draft knowledge entry - static dependency with versioned symbols plus
#   a consumer-generated version script makes lld report
#   "has undefined version"; switch the dependency to shared
# Source package: qatlib/26.02.0
#====================================================================

id:                     DRAFT-ohos-qatlib-26.02.0-static-libnuma-versioned-symbols-lld
trigger_tool:           ld.lld|clang|libtool|cmake|autotools
phase:                  link|build

error_signature:        has undefined version libnuma_1.1|has undefined version libnuma_1.2|symbol numa_node_to_cpus@@libnuma_1\.2 has undefined version|ld\.lld: error: .*\.a\(.*\.o\): symbol .*@.*has undefined version

severity:               2
category:               linking|symbol-versioning|conan-dependencies|static-vs-shared
match_keywords:         OHOS, ld.lld, undefined version, versioned symbol, symbol versioning, version-script, export-symbols-regex, libtool, static library, libnuma, numactl, qatlib, shared
title:                  Static dependency symbols carrying version tags plus a consumer version script make lld fail with "has undefined version"

root_cause:             A static library may be built with GNU symbol versioning, so its
                        members carry version tags (numa_node_to_cpus@@libnuma_1.2,
                        numa_max_possible_node@libnuma_1.1).  A static archive does not
                        carry the matching version DEFINITIONS - those normally live in
                        a shared object's .gnu.version_d, written when linking the .so
                        against a version script.  When the consumer also generates its
                        own version script (qatlib does via libtool's
                        -export-symbols-regex '^(qae)'), lld switches into versioned
                        symbol resolution and requires every referenced version name to
                        have a definition.  libnuma_1.1 / libnuma_1.2 are defined nowhere
                        and no shared library supplies them, so lld emits
                        "has undefined version" for each such symbol - 20 lines in this
                        package.

affected_scope:         Any project on OHOS that links a static archive built with
                        symbol versioning while itself producing a version script.
                        Measured on qatlib 26.02.0 against ohpcd's static-only
                        numactl/2.0.18.

verification_cmd:       make -j4 LIBS=-lnuma 2>&1 | grep -c "undefined version"

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           use-shared-variant-of-that-dependency
rec_description:        Switch the offending dependency to its shared variant.
                        A shared libnuma.so carries the version definitions itself
                        (libnuma_1.1 / libnuma_1.2 nodes), so lld resolves them and the
                        consumer's version script no longer conflicts.  In Conan this is
                        a recipe option: "numactl/*:shared": True.  If the registry only
                        publishes a static build (as ohpcd's numactl/2.0.18 does), the
                        shared build must be produced first.
rec_command:            cmake -S <src> -B <build> -o numactl/*:shared=True   # or conan -o numactl/*:shared=True
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               conan-option

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      declare-version-nodes-in-consumer-script
fallback_description:   If the dependency cannot be made shared, declare the referenced
                        version names as empty nodes in the consumer's version script:
                        "libnuma_1.1 { }; libnuma_1.2 { }; VERS_x.y { global: qae*;
                        local: *; };"  Verified to link.  Costly in practice because the
                        script is auto-generated by libtool, so the injection point is
                        fragile - prefer priority 1.
fallback_command:       clang ... -Wl,-version-script -Wl,vs.map -shared -o v.so
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          version-script-edit

forbid_1_pattern:       --undefined-version as the fix|-Wl,--undefined-version .*resolved
forbid_1_reason:        Measured NOT to work here.  With LDFLAGS set at make time the flag
                        never reached the link line; after re-configuring so it did appear
                        in the libtool link command, all 20 errors persisted.  Only
                        switching to shared produced BUILD_RC=0.
forbid_1_consequence:   Two wasted rebuild cycles believing the link was fixed, while the
                        errors remain byte-identical.

forbid_2_pattern:       remove -export-symbols-regex|drop consumer version script
forbid_2_reason:        The version script intentionally narrows the exported ABI
                        surface; deleting it changes the package's public symbols.
forbid_2_consequence:   Silently widens the ABI beyond what upstream intended.

forbid_3_pattern:       link static libnuma\.a via system_libs|-lnuma.*static fallback
forbid_3_reason:        The static archive is the trigger; adding it another way
                        reproduces the same version-definition gap.
forbid_3_consequence:   Persistence of the same error under a different recipe line.

similar_to:             [E104, E341, E494, E266]
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

notes_negative_result:  The negative result is the point of this entry.  The intuitive
                        flag (-Wl,--undefined-version) was applied two different ways and
                        failed both times, with the flag confirmed present on the real
                        libtool link line in attempt 2.  Reproducible evidence:
                        qat-make5/6/7.log each contain undefined-version=20 with
                        MAKE_RC=2, while qat-make8.log (shared numactl) has
                        undefined-version=0 and MAKE_RC=0.
notes_single_vs_double: Both the single-@ and double-@@ forms appear:
                        numa_max_possible_node@libnuma_1.1 (introduced in that version)
                        and numa_node_to_cpus@@libnuma_1.2 (current default definition).
                        A fix must satisfy both.
notes_family_covered:   Three other qatlib gaps are NOT covered here because the
                        repository already documents the same patterns for
                        x86-only upstreams: SSE2 inline asm branches needing a non-x86
                        memcpy fallback (adf_memcpy64/128), the glibc-only
                        __GLIBC_PREREQ macro needing a false fallback, and pthread_t
                        being a pointer with musl-style libcs while the code treats it as
                        an integer.
notes_status:           Measured on qatlib 26.02.0: configure rc=0, make rc=0,
                        make install rc=0; consumer test 8/8 assertions pass.
